Well, I finally found a floor with a priestess (1st one in 19 levels, as usual
on my system (someone has got to fix the randomizer or something)) and wouldn't
you know it, the priestess is the wrong alignment (She's lawful, I'm neutral).
Since I have a polymorph and a polymorph control ring, I decide to try the
Leprechaun scam and see how it works.  I put on the ring, it asks me what I
want, sez I'm a new man, gets a new name from me, and that's it.  I don't
change into the monster or anything.  It doesn't happen with any monster I've
tried.  I've taken off all armour, magic protection, etc, with no luck.

Then, I went up 1 level, and I changed fine.  Then I went back down, and on my
way over to the priestess, it asked me againwhat I wanted to be.  I picked
leprechaun again, and ZAM, I was back to being normal.  Any ideas?
So I try again, and get to the priestess more quickly.  Stealing the gold works
OK.  Later on, I found out that a new intrinsic was added to me: "Bad luck does
not time out for you".  I am carrying a blessed luckstone, though, and still
have the "good luck does not..." message as well.  Another time, I saw I had
dropped 5 levels or so soon after I had chatted with the priestess.  Is the 
alignment difference the reason why?

Do you always lose 1 pt of CON when getting polymorphed?

Any ideas/suggestions would be appreciated.
